From 578e7502b5aa5563a5b52a295b2187740db1695c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:21:30 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] kcm_kwin_virtualdesktops: desktop list first, switching
 options in two noun sections; animation scan no longer runs twice
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: List (ScrollViewKCM, desktop list) with a Form footer. D-Bus calls to org.kde.KWin.VirtualDesktopManager,
kcfg keys and defaults unchanged. NOT BUILT YET.

Moved / renamed (footer FormLayout):
- "Options:" label gone; sections "Switching" (Navigation wraps around, Switch desktops independently for each screen,
  Show animation when switching + indented animation combo, Configure…, About) and "On-screen display" (Show on-screen
  display when switching, indented Show desktop layout indicators, "Hide after:" spin box).
- Checkbox texts lost their trailing colons ("Show animation when switching", "Show on-screen display when switching");
  the combo + buttons moved to their own row under the parent checkbox (dependent options indented); the animation
  Configure… button got a text, the About button an Accessible.name and tooltip; combo got an Accessible.name.
  The hide-delay spin box got the label "Hide after:" in place of sitting beside the checkbox.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-023, HIG-057. page-design.md 1, 2, 3, 6.

Speed cause (code evidence): AnimationsModel inherits EffectsModel::load (common/effectsmodel.cpp:373), which
synchronously scans built-in, JavaScript (KPackage) and plugin effects before posting the async areEffectsSupported
call; it ran twice before the first frame: VirtualDesktopsData ctor (virtualdesktopsdata.cpp:26) and again in
VirtualDesktops::load(). The first load() now skips the second scan (m_animationsModelLoaded); later loads (reset
after Apply) still reload. The remaining scan is still synchronous in the data ctor: moving it off the first frame
needs an async EffectsModel::load and was not attempted without a build. DesktopsModel D-Bus is already async.
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet. Unconfirmed: skipping the second load() has no side
effect on KCModuleData::loaded (emitted by the first load's commit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
